Z||000012||Racer 1||01-11-2001||09:10 PM||||Mine never have popped up even doing 120 mph. I can barely open mine with my hands. Maybe you need to adjust the doors towards the front of the car more.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://spitfire.cwv.net/~cdbailey/images/gifssucl/eyes2/evil_eyes.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000013||fropuff||01-11-2001||09:48 PM||||Is there a way to like use some nylon ties to fasten the door to a part of the headlight motor or to the car itself?  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000014||lowCG||01-11-2001||09:52 PM||||Mine do open at higher speeds,not at anything less than 120 though,so I probably won't be fixing them any time soon.<BR>Something I found out the hard way was that Fiero's are "bottom feeders" in that they get the air for the radiator off the road,not through the opening.I made a panel to go under the nose to keep the air out of there,and my 3.4 swap then stressed the cooling system enough to make it apparent at freeway speeds that there wasn't adequate airflow through the radiator.||||reg||1
Z||000015||RiceCooker||01-11-2001||09:52 PM||||Happened to me in Montana last year. I was goin bout 115mph. Thought I was gonna die! <P>My dad and I - actually it was just him - put a penny underneath the spring on each side. All this did was tighten the spring a bit but it worked. Later got the car up to top speed (130) and didn't have any problems. Got home and took them out cause I don't plan on going that fast again. <P>Beauty, eh?||||reg||6
