Z||000029||FIEROGOD||01-14-2001||08:53 PM|||| Yes my car also has this problem. It is a little different though. The driver side pops up first then the passenger one. It depends on how fast i am going and the wind speed, also the wind direction. Sometimes if i hit a huge dip in the road at extremely high speeds , that can also make them pop up.<BR>I seen an ad some where that reads "heavy-duty head light door springs, you will know if you need them". I don't know if that is the answer. I think that they would be to hard on the head light motors.<BR> My 87 blue sport-poop had a problem with the drivers side popping up. It would not go fast enough to get the passenger side to pop up. <BR> As far as the front-end floating, lower the car! ||||reg||12
